  "title": "Cleopatra VII",
  "summary": "Cleopatra VII Philopator was the final active monarch of the Ptolemaic Kingdom of Egypt, reigning from 51 to 30 BCE. Famed for her political acumen and multilingual diplomacy, she formed crucial alliances with Roman leaders Julius Caesar and Mark Antony to defend Egyptian sovereignty. Her defeat at Actium and subsequent suicide in 30 BCE ended three centuries of Ptolemaic rule and brought Egypt under direct Roman imperial administration.",
